# State protocol (always on)

Enforcer: `state_lint.py --repo .` (repo STATE files), `state_manager.py verify`, CI `state-check` (comment mode) and `state-files-gate` (block), the workstation git hooks (post-checkout, post-merge), the workstation-core skills (session-start, state-closeout, pr-closeout).

- Live state lives in the repo (workstation decision 2026-11-22, PR #114; ADR-2026-11-23-state-in-repo): `STATE.md` at the repo root on `main` = the single coordinator chat (changed only through the coordinator's PR); `STATE-<slug>.md` at the worktree root = one worker each, committed and pushed on its own branch (slug = branch name, lowercase, other characters as `-`; the post-checkout hook creates it); `BACKLOG.md` at the repo root, append only (close an item with a new `[closed <date>] <item>` line); `archives/` at the repo root. `state_paths.py --repo .` prints the state folder and the store notes folder.
- A PR's last commit archives its state file (`state_manager.py archive-branch` = `git mv STATE-<slug>.md archives/STATE-<slug>-<YYYYMMDD>.md`); CI `state-files-gate` blocks a PR that leaves a top-level `STATE-*.md`. The coordinator reads every branch's state with `state_manager.py branches --show`.
- The memory store (`<Projects>\_claude\Claude Projects\Working Memory\memory\custom-pdm\INDEX.md`) keeps notes only (preferences, machine facts, gotchas): no progress, open items, handoffs or STATE / BACKLOG there, and none in other repo files or memory notes.
- STATE schema v1, 30 lines max, overwritten each time; only `[NEXT]` lines stay in a STATE file. The root STATE Pointers may hold `Question_Counter`, `Last_Cleanup`, `Kept_Branches`; `Branch_States` is generated (`state_manager.py branches`), never typed.
- Seven tags: `[DONE]` (dropped: git history is the record), `[NEXT]` (stays), `[TASK]` (`TASK.md` of the branch), `[ADR]` (DECISIONS), `[RULE]` (`.claude/rules/<domain>.md` + rules_sync), `[SOT]` (data files, only after Dan's yes; until then a BACKLOG line marked `needs owner yes`), `[BKLG]` (BACKLOG). A line carried through two closeouts must graduate.
- Run state-closeout at 80 % context, on a pivot, a blocker, a milestone and every PR (pr-closeout writes the PR body `State:` line). Handoffs: `state-closeout handoff` prints a paste block; the STATE-<slug> file is the handoff.
- Workers write only their own `STATE-<slug>.md` (committed on their branch) and BACKLOG lines; the coordinator owns the root STATE, DECISIONS and the router. Every user answer goes to its home in the same turn, with the date.
- Finished deliverables (fab outputs, enclosure releases, drawings) are locked with `deliverable_lock.py` (`VERIFIED.lock`, `Last_Verified_SHA` in STATE); a locked file that changed without Dan's unlock is a regression (regression-restore).
- Never do: leave a question ID without its text (L1 had to be dug out of git history, 2026-11); put one session's questions into another session's list.
